    <bpmn:process id="W_W1328" name="W1328. Third-Party Risk Assessment &amp; Vendor Criticality Tiering" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual vendor criticality review cycle; new vendor relationship above PHP 10M annual spend; vendor financial distress signal (payment default, news report, credit rating downgrade); or post-incident review revealing over-reliance on a single vendor
Frequency: Annual full review of top-200 vendors by spend; quarterly monitoring of Critical-tier vendors; ad-hoc for trigger events
Volume: ~200 vendors reviewed annually (top vendors by spend representing ~85% of COGS); ~20–30 vendors re-tiered per cycle
Owner: Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)
Participants: Category Manager, Procurement Director, CFO, VP Supply Chain, CIO (for technology vendor dependencies)
Source: workflow W1328 — Third-Party Risk Assessment &amp; Vendor Criticality Tiering</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1328_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1328_Lane1" name="Procurement Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1328_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1328_Lane3" name="Head of IA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1328_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1328_Start5" name="Annual vendor criticality review cycle; new vendor relationship above PHP 10M annual…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task6" name="Vendor spend &amp; dependency analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Vendor spend &amp; dependency analysis: Procurement extracts annual vendor spend data and category assignment: (a) identify sole-source vendors (only one approved vendor for a category), (b) identify single-source vendors (one primary vendor supplying &gt; 80% of category volume despite alternates existing), (c) calculate concentration ratio: top-5 vendor spend ÷ total COGS, (d) identify vendor-to-store dependency: are all 200 stores equally dependent on the vendor, or do certain regions rely more heavily?
Responsible (R): Procurement Analyst
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task7" name="Financial health assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Financial health assessment: For vendors above PHP 10M annual spend: (a) request audited financial statements (or BIR-filed financials for Philippine vendors), (b) calculate financial risk indicators: current ratio, debt-to-equity, revenue trend (3-year), profit margin trend, (c) check SEC registration status and any regulatory actions for Philippine corporations, (d) for import vendors: check country risk rating (using World Bank/Economist Intelligence Unit data), sanctions list screening, and political stability indicators, (e) assign financial health score: Green (low risk), Yellow (moderate — declining trend), Red (high — immediate concern)
Responsible (R): Procurement Analyst / Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task8" name="Operational resilience assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Operational resilience assessment: For vendors Critical-tiered in the prior cycle plus current sole/single-source candidates: (a) assess geographic concentration: is the vendor&#x27;s manufacturing facility in a typhoon-prone area, or near a single port?, (b) assess capacity utilization: does the vendor have surge capacity for BuildRight&#x27;s peak demand (pre-summer, pre-Ber months)?, (c) assess logistics dependency: does the vendor rely on a single shipping route or port that could be disrupted?, (d) assess technology dependency: for IT vendors, does BuildRight have data portability and system access if the vendor fails?, (e) assess regulatory exposure: is the vendor in a heavily regulated industry (DENR permits for cement plants, FDA for paints/coatings) with risk of forced shutdown?
Responsible (R): Category Manager / CIO (for IT vendors)
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task9" name="Criticality tiering">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Criticality tiering: Head of IA assigns criticality tier based on spend, dependency, financial health, and operational resilience: Tier 1 — Critical (sole-source for essential category OR single-source &gt; 80% OR annual spend &gt; PHP 500M OR vendor failure would stop sales in multiple stores within 2 weeks); Tier 2 — High (significant spend PHP 100M–500M, limited alternate sources, category impact if disrupted); Tier 3 — Moderate (moderate spend PHP 20M–100M, alternates available but switching takes 30–60 days); Tier 4 — Low (spend &lt; PHP 20M, multiple alternates, easy substitution)
Responsible (R): Head of IA
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task10" name="Mitigation plan development">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Mitigation plan development: For Tier 1 and Tier 2 vendors: Category Manager develops risk mitigation plan: (a) Dual-sourcing strategy: identify and qualify at least one alternate vendor per critical category per W224; timeline: 6–12 months for qualification, (b) Safety stock policy: increase safety stock for critical sole-source items per W31 to cover 30–60 days of demand, (c) Contractual protections: include business continuity clause, disaster recovery commitment, and termination-for-convenience provision in vendor agreements per W688, (d) Monitoring cadence: quarterly financial health check for Tier 1, semi-annual for Tier 2, (e) Escalation protocol: pre-defined triggers for activating alternate sourcing (vendor misses OTIF for 2 consecutive months, vendor credit rating downgraded, natural disaster at vendor location)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 days per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1328_Task11" name="Board risk committee reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Board risk committee reporting: Head of IA includes third-party risk summary in quarterly ERM review per W122: (a) number of Critical/High-tier vendors and concentration ratio, (b) key risks and mitigation status for top-10 critical vendors, (c) any trigger events during the quarter and response actions, (d) progress on dual-sourcing initiatives for sole-source categories, (e) recommendation for Board approval if vendor risk acceptance decision required (e.g., accepting sole-source risk due to insufficient alternate quality)
Responsible (R): Head of IA
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Absorbed into W122 quarterly cycle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1328_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1328_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1328_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1328_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-305 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Risk Management (PA-21.2).) | - operational: requiring minimum financial documentation (BIR-filed income statement) as a vendor portal condition per W705
Owner: Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1328_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1328_Annotation13" targetRef="W1328_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1328_Flow15" sourceRef="W1328_Start5" targetRef="W1328_Task6" />
