    <bpmn:process id="W_W1461" name="W1461. Supply Chain Disruption Risk Monitoring &amp; Geopolitical Alert Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Real-time supply chain disruption alert; or weekly supply chain risk dashboard review
Frequency: Continuous monitoring; weekly dashboard review; ad-hoc disruption response
Volume: ~5–10 significant alerts/month; 1–2 requiring executive response per quarter
Owner: VP Supply Chain
Participants: VP Supply Chain, Import Coordinator, VP Supply Chain, Category Managers, DC Managers, Treasury Analyst
Source: workflow W1461 — Supply Chain Disruption Risk Monitoring &amp; Geopolitical Alert Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1461_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1461_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1461_Lane2" name="VP Supply Chain">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1461_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1461_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1461_Start5" name="Real-time supply chain disruption alert; or weekly supply chain risk dashboard review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1461_Task6" name="Continuous monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Continuous monitoring: System aggregates risk signals: port congestion (PPA, ATI, ICTSI), PAGASA weather alerts, geopolitical feeds, supplier financial health (top 20 vendors = 45% COGS), shipping lane disruptions, fuel price alerts; classify Level 1–3 severity
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1461_Task7" name="Level 3 assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Level 3 assessment: Assess impact scope (categories, DCs, stores, duration); check safety stock; convene rapid response call with Category Managers and DC Managers
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1461_Task8" name="Alternative sourcing activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Alternative sourcing activation: Identify alternative suppliers; evaluate air vs. sea freight; approve premium freight; confirm FX with Treasury; issue emergency PO per W2
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Import Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1461_Task9" name="Inventory triage &amp; allocation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inventory triage &amp; allocation: Constrained inventory report; allocation governance per W105 (prioritize low-stock stores and B2B accounts); emergency inter-DC transfers per W218
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 2–3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1461_Task10" name="Weekly risk dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly risk dashboard: Present to VP Supply Chain and COO: active disruptions, 30-day outlook, inventory health, sourcing status, cost impact
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1461_Task11" name="Post-disruption review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-disruption review: After-action review; update risk register per W122; adjust safety stock; update vendor diversification
Responsible (R): VP Supply Chain
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 4–8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1461_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1461_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1461_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1461_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-305 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Risk Management (PA-21.2).) | - operational: VP Supply Chain review and approval gate
Owner: VP Supply Chain</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1461_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1461_Annotation13" targetRef="W1461_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
