    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1541" name="W1541. Key Risk Indicator (KRI) Monthly Monitoring, Threshold Alert &amp; Risk Appetite Dashboard Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly KRI reporting cycle (aligned with month-end close); or KRI threshold breach alert
Frequency: Monthly review; continuous monitoring with automated alerts
Volume: ~40–50 KRIs across 8 risk categories
Owner: Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Participants: Internal Audit Head, Risk Analyst, CFO, COO, CEO
Source: workflow W1541 — Key Risk Indicator (KRI) Monthly Monitoring, Threshold Alert &amp; Risk Appetite Dashboard Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1541_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1541_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1541_Lane2" name="Responsible VP">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1541_Lane3" name="Risk Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1541_Lane4" name="Internal Audit Head">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1541_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1541_Start6" name="Monthly KRI reporting cycle (aligned with month-end close); or KRI threshold breach alert">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1541_Task7" name="KRI data collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: KRI data collection: System automatically extracts KRI data from source systems — shrinkage from inventory/WMS, supplier delivery from procurement, cyber incidents from IT security (W367), employee turnover from HR (W43), safety incidents from HSE (W140), cash variance from POS/financials (W958); Risk Analyst reviews data quality and completeness
Responsible (R): System / Risk Analyst
Accountable (A): Internal Audit Head
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1541_Task8" name="Threshold comparison">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Threshold comparison: System compares each KRI against three thresholds: (a) Green (within normal range — risk within appetite), (b) Amber (approaching risk appetite limit — management attention required), (c) Red (breached risk appetite limit — immediate escalation required); thresholds calibrated annually during strategic planning (W127)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1541_Task9" name="Alert distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Alert distribution: For any KRI in Amber or Red status, system distributes automated alerts — Amber: email to responsible VP with KRI detail, trend chart, and recommended actions; Red: SMS + email to responsible VP and CEO with mandatory response requirement within 48 hours
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1541_Task10" name="Root cause investigation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Root cause investigation (Red KRIs): For Red-status KRIs, responsible VP initiates root cause investigation within 48 hours — determines if breach is a one-time spike or systemic trend; documents findings and corrective action plan; Internal Audit may initiate focused audit (W121) if warranted
Responsible (R): Responsible VP / Risk Analyst
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 4–8 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1541_Task11" name="Monthly KRI dashboard">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly KRI dashboard: Risk Analyst compiles monthly KRI dashboard — all KRIs with current status (Green/Amber/Red), trend vs. prior 3 months, risk appetite utilization percentage, top 5 risk concerns, corrective action status for previously escalated items; dashboard presented to executive risk committee
Responsible (R): Risk Analyst
Accountable (A): Internal Audit Head
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1541_Task12" name="Quarterly risk appetite review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly risk appetite review: Internal Audit Head facilitates quarterly review with CEO and CFO — assess whether risk appetite thresholds are set appropriately based on actual experience; adjust thresholds if needed; review emerging risks not yet captured in KRI framework; update risk register (W122)
Responsible (R): Internal Audit Head
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 3 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1541_Task13" name="Annual KRI framework refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual KRI framework refresh: As part of annual strategic planning (W127), Internal Audit Head reviews the full KRI framework — add new KRIs for emerging risks, retire KRIs no longer relevant, recalibrate thresholds based on cumulative data, align with industry benchmarks
Responsible (R): Internal Audit Head
Accountable (A): Board Audit Committee
Duration: 16 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1541_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1541_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
