    <bpmn:process id="W_W5501" name="W5501. Climate Physical &amp; Transition Risk Assessment, Scenario Analysis &amp; Resilience Response Planning" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Annual ERM cycle (quarterly risk committee per W122); (b) material climate event post-mortem (typhoon, flood, ashfall); (c) disclosure cycle (VS-25.3) or lender/sustainable-finance questionnaire
Frequency: Full assessment annual; scenario refresh annual; event-driven interim updates
Volume: ~205 exposed sites (200 stores + 4 DCs + HQ) geo-coded against hazard layers; ~400–600 import TEUs/month of supply-lane exposure (VS-122); ~800–1,000 vendors (VS-161); insurance schedule of ~205 properties (VS-26); 10–15-year scenario horizon
Owner: Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)
Participants: ESG/Sustainability Manager (VS-25), Property/Real Estate (VS-97/VS-20), Treasury &amp; Insurance (VS-26), Supply Chain Planning (VS-02/VS-127), Network Design (VS-136), Facilities &amp; Energy (VS-138/VS-120), Merchandising/Commodity (VS-106), CFO, external catastrophe-modeling advisers
Source: workflow W5501 — Climate Physical &amp; Transition Risk Assessment, Scenario Analysis &amp; Resilience Response Planning</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5501_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5501_Lane1" name="Risk Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5501_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5501_Start3" name="(a) Annual ERM cycle (quarterly risk committee per W122); (b) material climate event…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task4" name="Scope &amp; governance: register climate as a named ERM risk domain with separate…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Scope &amp; governance: register climate as a named ERM risk domain with separate physical- and transition-risk appetite statements; integrate into the W122 review calendar and risk register taxonomy
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / ESG Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 days (initial); thereafter annual refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task5" name="Hazard exposure mapping: geo-code all sites/DCs in the location master (VS-29)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Hazard exposure mapping: geo-code all sites/DCs in the location master (VS-29) and overlay Philippine hazard layers (PAGASA/NOAH-type flood &amp; wind, PHIVOLCS fault/ashfall, storm-surge and sea-level for coastal sites); map import lanes and vendor geography (VS-122/VS-161); produce site-level exposure tiers (High/Medium/Low)
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / Network Design / External Advisor
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)
Duration: 8–12 days (initial); 2–3 days/year refresh</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task6" name="Scenario definition: minimum two physical scenarios (severe-typhoon…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Scenario definition: minimum two physical scenarios (severe-typhoon amplification/high-warming vs. moderate) and two transition scenarios (accelerated policy &amp; energy-price stress vs. gradual), calibrated to the Philippine context over a 10–15-year horizon; document assumptions and data sources
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / ESG / External Advisor
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–5 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task7" name="Impact quantification per scenario: store damage and business-interruption days…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Impact quantification per scenario: store damage and business-interruption days vs. sums insured and BI cover (W862/W1565); revenue loss by region; reconstruction capex (VS-184 benchmarks); supply disruption and lead-time inflation (VS-02.3 W558/W729); commodity/input cost swings (VS-106); energy cost paths (VS-120); logistics rerouting cost (VS-136/VS-06)
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / Finance / Supply Chain
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 8–10 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task8" name="Vulnerability &amp; adaptation assessment: roof/wind-uplift and flood standards for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Vulnerability &amp; adaptation assessment: roof/wind-uplift and flood standards for remodels and new stores (VS-109/VS-37/VS-20); DC flood-proofing and stock elevation (VS-04); backup power coverage (VS-108 renewables+storage; generator posture W470); inventory positioning and safety-stock policy (VS-136 MEIO); critical-vendor resilience (VS-161 stress tests)
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / Property / Facilities / Network Design
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 5–8 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task9" name="Response &amp; mitigation planning: feed prioritized resilience-capex proposals…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Response &amp; mitigation planning: feed prioritized resilience-capex proposals into capital governance (VS-40); adjust insurance program at renewal (W862 — limits, deductibles, BI indemnity periods); update BCP and protocols (W847; ashfall W1449; earthquake W1450; typhoon VS-69); commission transition mitigation (VS-108 generation, VS-120 efficiency, VS-192 fleet)
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / Treasury / BCP / Property
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 5–8 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task10" name="Disclosure integration: outputs feed climate/ESG disclosure (VS-25.3…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Disclosure integration: outputs feed climate/ESG disclosure (VS-25.3 TCFD/ISSB-aligned W694/W1334), lender and sustainable-finance questionnaires, and board risk reporting through the committee pack (W1721) with governance-level physical/transition summary
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / ESG
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 3–4 days/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5501_Task11" name="KRIs, monitoring &amp; re-run: maintain site-exposure-tier register and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: KRIs, monitoring &amp; re-run: maintain site-exposure-tier register and hazard-season dashboard as KRIs on the W1329/W1541 apparatus; post-event loss-vs-model reconciliation after each material event (VS-69.3/VS-184 actuals); annual re-run adjusts tiers, scenarios, and mitigation backlog
Responsible (R): Risk Officer / Analytics
Accountable (A): Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter + per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5501_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5501_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5501_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5501_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-305 (ensure controlled execution — Enterprise Risk Management (PA-21.2).)
Owner: Head of Internal Audit (acting as Risk Officer)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5501_Assoc14" sourceRef="W5501_Annotation13" targetRef="W5501_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
